WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.892
In this example, website visits are separated by user and ordered by visit time.

00:00:05.892 --> 00:00:13.754
The next-value function, written L E A D in the code, brings the next visit timestamp onto the current row.

00:00:14.204 --> 00:00:19.546
We can then subtract the current visit time from the next visit time to measure the gap.

00:00:19.546 --> 00:00:25.786
The final visit for each user has no later visit, so the next value is null.

00:00:25.786 --> 00:00:27.556
That is not an error.

00:00:27.556 --> 00:00:30.119
It simply means the sequence ends there.
